# ~/.cache is removed and symbolicly linked to /tmp/.unburden-<user1>/cache/.
# This covers Google Chrome cache, used by most users. At first we tried  "m D
# .cache cache" to move instead of remove the folder, but the result was that
# the first time a user logged in after this change, it took minutes with a
# blank screen to move the files from NFS to the local hard disk, and that
# confused and irritated the user.

r D .cache cache
